  "worked_solution": "Let $u=sin\u2061x$ and $v=x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =cos\u2061x\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}-u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(cos\u2061x)-sin\u2061x\\cdot (1)}{(x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{xcos\u2061x-sin\u2061x}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
